UID:recur-ucl-gatsby@research
DTSTAMP:20260101T000000Z
DTSTART:20260104T090000
DTEND:20260104T100000
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:CHECK: UCL Gatsby Unit Research Internship (January round\, exact d
 ate TBC)
DESCRIPTION:Minimum stage: Advanced undergraduate (about 3rd year or later)
 \nEligibility: Final-year undergraduates and Master's students. The intern
 ship is not part of a degree.\nDeadline: The unit reviews applications in 
 January and July. For summer internships\, apply by the January deadline. 
 The exact 2027 date is not published yet\, so the date shown is a reminder
  to check the Vacancies page\, not a deadline.\nRequirements: Earlier call
 s asked for a CV (2 pages) and transcripts.\nBenefits: Paid research inter
 nship (earlier calls: up to 3 months).\nNote: The Gatsby Bridging Programm
 e is a separate 7-week maths summer school for penultimate- or final-year 
 undergraduates and Master's students.\nPortal: https://www.ucl.ac.uk/life-
 sciences/gatsby/study-and-work
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-P14D
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: CHECK: UCL Gatsby Unit Research Internship (January r
 ound\, exact date TBC) in 14 days
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-P3D
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Urgent: CHECK: UCL Gatsby Unit Research Internship (January rou
 nd\, exact date TBC) in 3 days
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:recur-weidenfeld-hoffmann@research
DTSTAMP:20260101T000000Z
DTSTART:20260106T090000
DTEND:20260106T100000
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:DEADLINE: Weidenfeld-Hoffmann Scholarships & Leadership Programme (
 Oxford master's\, 2027-28)
DESCRIPTION:Minimum stage: Graduate (Bachelor's completed\, or Master's/PhD
  student)\nEligibility: Graduates and early-career professionals from main
 ly low- and middle-income countries\; must be admitted to an eligible 1-ye
 ar Oxford master's course (no DPhil) and intend to return to their home co
 untry or region. Most scholars have 5+ years of work experience\, but it i
 s not required. Check Oxford's lists of eligible countries and courses.\nB
 enefits: 100% of course fees\, a living stipend (£21\,805 in 2026-27) and
  a place on the Leadership Programme (about 200 hours\, mid-September to e
 arly July).\nDeadline: Set by the Oxford course: the January deadline or e
 arlier (some courses close in December). The date shown is a typical Janua
 ry date\, so check your course page.\nRequirements: Select the scholarship
  on the Oxford graduate application form and submit the WHT application at
  the same time\; English language test required.\nPortal: https://whtrust.
 org/scholarship-application/
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-P14D
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: DEADLINE: Weidenfeld-Hoffmann Scholarships & Leadersh
 ip Programme (Oxford master's\, 2027-28) in 14 days
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-P3D
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Urgent: DEADLINE: Weidenfeld-Hoffmann Scholarships & Leadership
  Programme (Oxford master's\, 2027-28) in 3 days
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
