RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:DEADLINE: Caltech SURF (Summer Undergraduate Research)
DESCRIPTION:Minimum stage: Undergraduate\nFocus: Research in any field offe
 red at Caltech\, including computing\, AI and algorithms (placement depend
 s on your mentor).\nEligibility: Continuing undergraduates\, international
  students included. Caltech students need a GPA of 2.0+\; visiting student
 s need a cumulative GPA of 2.5/4.0+ and must be eligible for fall registra
 tion. JPL placements are limited to US citizens and permanent residents.\n
 Benefits: 10-week fellowship starting mid-June with a flat stipend\, about
  $8\,110 in 2026. The 2027 amount and exactly what it covers are not confi
 rmed here\, so check the official page.\nRequirements: A Caltech faculty m
 entor's agreement to supervise you\, research proposal\, unofficial transc
 ript\, 2 recommendation letters (at least one from a faculty member)\, onl
 ine application.\nDeadline: Applications open Nov 1\, 2026\; application a
 nd letters due Feb 22\, 2027\; awards announced Apr 1\, 2027.\nPortal: htt
 ps://sfp.caltech.edu/undergraduate-research/programs/surf/application_info
 rmation
