 r Biological Cybernetics and Intelligent Systems and the Tübingen AI Cent
 er.\nEligibility: Bachelor's and Master's students worldwide. The programm
 e specifically targets motivated students constrained by personal\, financ
 ial\, regional or societal issues that affect their future education\, and
  applicants are expected to explain how access to first-class education is
  constrained for them. Students from low- and middle-income countries are 
 explicitly encouraged to apply. Students without a finished Bachelor's nee
 d at least 4 completed semesters (earlier years counted them at applicatio
 n\, the 2026 page before the internship starts\, so check the 2027 call).\
 nProgram: Paid 3-month research internship\, Jul 1 to Sep 30\, 2027. You m
 ust be available for the full period\, and it must be voluntary rather tha
 n for course credit. The coordination office arranges affordable accommoda
 tion. The exact stipend and travel support are not confirmed here.\nDeadli
 ne: Nov 16\, 2026 (portal opened Oct 21\; interviews in January\, notifica
 tions in February). No application fee.\nPortal: https://www.projects.tueb
 ingen.mpg.de/
